<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Choros (Oirats)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Choros are a clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and one of the four main groups of the Four Oirat confederation. In the 17th century their leaders founded and ruled the Dzungar Khanate, which dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> until the Qing conquest of 1755 to 1758. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esen-taishi">Esen Taishi</a>, who briefly ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> in the 15th century, also belonged to the Choros.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/choros-oirats.jpg" alt="Choros (Oirats)" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khiruge · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Oirat_Confederation.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
